{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013hG1xynwq24d1FZgv8CXfw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd084-link\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/link: Create a Hard Link\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  The link utility creates a single hard link using the link(2) system call, unlike ln\n6\t  which supports multiple targets, symlinks, and directory handling. macOS ships link but\n7\t  the Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (glink, installed\n8\t  by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Create a hard link from FILE1 to FILE2 using the link(2) system call.\n12\t  - G2: Verify functional parity against glink via differential testing.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: Hard link creation\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: Must accept exactly two arguments FILE1 and FILE2 and create a hard link at FILE2 pointing to FILE1 using the link(2) system call.\n20\t      - R1.2:\n21\t          text: Must not follow symlinks, create symlinks, or handle directories specially — the raw link(2) semantics apply.\n22\t      - R1.3:\n23\t          text: Must exit 1 with an error to stderr if fewer or more than two arguments are given.\n24\t      - R1.4:\n25\t          text: Must exit 1 with an error to stderr if the link(2) call fails (e.g., FILE1 does not exist, FILE2 already exists, cross-device link).\n26\t\n27\t  R2:\n28\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n29\t    items:\n30\t      - R2.1:\n31\t          text: Must exit 0 when the hard link is created successfully.\n32\t      - R2.2:\n33\t          text: Must exit 1 on any error.\n34\t      - R2.3:\n35\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n36\t\n37\tnon_goals:\n38\t  - cmd/link does not support symbolic links; use ln -s for that.\n39\t  - cmd/link does not support multiple targets or directory handling; use ln for that.\n40\t\n41\tacceptance_criteria:\n42\t  - id: AC1\n43\t    criterion: \"link file1 file2 creates a hard link at file2, matching glink behavior.\"\n44\t    traces:\n45\t      - R1.1\n46\t      - R1.2\n47\t  - id: AC2\n48\t    criterion: \"link with wrong number of arguments exits 1 with usage error, matching glink.\"\n49\t    traces:\n50\t      - R1.3\n51\t  - id: AC3\n52\t    criterion: \"Differential test against glink passes for all required test cases.\"\n53\t    traces:\n54\t      - R1.1\n55\t      - R1.2\n56\t      - R1.3\n57\t      - R1.4\n58\t  - id: AC4\n59\t    criterion: \"cmd/link compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n60\t    traces:\n61\t      - R1.1\n62\t      - R1.2\n63\t      - R1.3\n64\t      - R1.4\n65\t      - R2.1\n66\t      - R2.2\n67\t      - R2.3\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1263d149-1945-4237-840f-ed4beb03006d","uuid":"43a20bd1-3c5a-490d-95ca-73509e170f78","timestamp":"2026-05-23T12:32:32.416Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5528/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd084-link.yaml","content":"id: srd084-link\ntitle: \"cmd/link: Create a Hard Link\"\n\nproblem: |\n  The link utility creates a single hard link using the link(2) system call, unlike ln\n  which supports multiple targets, symlinks, and directory handling. macOS ships link but\n  the Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (glink, installed\n  by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Create a hard link from FILE1 to FILE2 using the link(2) system call.\n  - G2: Verify functional parity against glink via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Hard link creation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must accept exactly two arguments FILE1 and FILE2 and create a hard link at FILE2 pointing to FILE1 using the link(2) system call.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must not follow symlinks, create symlinks, or handle directories specially — the raw link(2) semantics apply.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must exit 1 with an error to stderr if fewer or more than two arguments are given.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 with an error to stderr if the link(2) call fails (e.g., FILE1 does not exist, FILE2 already exists, cross-device link).\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when the hard link is created successfully.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/link does not support symbolic links; use ln -s for that.\n  - cmd/link does not support multiple targets or directory handling; use ln for that.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"link file1 file2 creates a hard link at file2, matching glink behavior.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"link with wrong number of arguments exits 1 with usage error, matching glink.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against glink passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/link compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n","numLines":68,"startLine":1,"totalLines":68}}}
