{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler/stitch task (Task ID: 5528) to implement `cmd/link/main.go` for the go-unix-utils project. This is a Go utility that creates hard links via the `link(2)` system call. The task requires implementing srd084 requirements R2.1 (exit 0 on success), R2.2 (exit 1 on error), and R2.3 (SIGPIPE handling via pkg/sys), along with the core link creation logic (R1.1), argument validation (R1.3), and error reporting (R1.4). The task follows strict constraints: no git commands, no filesystem exploration, only create `cmd/link/main.go`, follow the project's go_style_constitution and execution_constitution.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go `os.Link(oldname, newname)` wrapping the `link(2)` system call for hard link creation\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - all cmd/ utilities must call this at start of main()\n   - Differential testing pattern against GNU reference binary (`glink` from Homebrew coreutils)\n   - GNU coreutils-compatible error message formatting\n   - SPDX copyright header required on all Go files\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max per function (E8)\n   - No git commands allowed - orchestrator manages git externally\n   - Write all code before building/testing - no incremental compile-fix loops\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd084-link.yaml` (READ)\n     - The SRD defining all requirements for the link utility\n     - Key requirements: R1.1 (two args, link(2)), R1.2 (no symlink following), R1.3 (argument validation), R1.4 (link failure error), R2.1 (exit 0 success), R2.2 (exit 1 error), R2.3 (SIGPIPE)\n     - Non-goals: no symbolic links, no multiple targets, no directory handling\n   \n   - `cmd/unlink/main.go` (READ - reference pattern)\n     - This is the template pattern for implementing cmd/link\n     - Full code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"syscall\"\n     \n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const helpText = `Usage: unlink FILE\n       or:  unlink OPTION\n     Call the unlink function to remove the specified FILE.\n     \n           --help     display this help and exit\n           --version  output version information and exit\n     `\n     \n     const versionText = `unlink (go-unix-utils) dev\n     `\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             switch arg {\n             case \"--help\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case \"--version\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             }\n         }\n         if len(args) == 0 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"unlink: missing operand\\n\")\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'unlink --help' for more information.\\n\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         if len(args) > 1 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"unlink: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[1])\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'unlink --help' for more information.\\n\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         if err := syscall.Unlink(args[0]); err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"unlink: cannot unlink '%s': %s\\n\", args[0], capitalizeErr(err))\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func capitalizeErr(err error) string {\n         msg := err.Error()\n         if len(msg) > 0 {\n             return strings.ToUpper(msg